# Start or stop the exterior follow-camera recording.
#
# One service rather than two, because start and stop are the same concern and a caller that
# can reach one can always reach the other. `path` is written by the SIDECAR, not the caller,
# so it resolves on the machine running the simulator.
#
# Deliberately separate from the onboard capture path: that one feeds the model and is a
# measurement surface, this one is a spectator and is scored on nothing. Recording must never
# be able to fail a flight.
bool start                      # false = stop, and the remaining fields are ignored
string path                     # absolute .mp4 path; the sidecar creates parent directories
int32 width
int32 height
float64 fps
---
bool success
int32 frames                    # on stop: what was actually written
int32 dropped                   # frames the follower could not keep up with
float64 seconds
string message
